#: data/io.github.nacho.fastmath.metainfo.xml:19
msgid ""
"Fast Math is a game to train your mental arithmetic. Pick the operations you "
"want to practice, choose a level and answer up to 60 questions before the "
"time runs out."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.nacho.fastmath.metainfo.xml:24
msgid ""
"Choose any combination of addition, subtraction, multiplication and "
"division, and mix them in the same round. Pick one of five levels and set "
"the time limit, which is two minutes by default. Type each answer and press "
"Enter. At the end you see how many answers you got right and how fast you "
"were, and the best scores are kept in a leaderboard."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.nacho.fastmath.metainfo.xml:31
msgid ""
"The comparison mode asks whether a number is less than, equal to or greater "
"than another. Compare whole numbers, decimals like 8.3 and 8.25, fractions "
"like 1/3 and 1/4, or calculations, alone or mixed."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.nacho.fastmath.metainfo.xml:36
msgid ""
"The fractions mode shows a pizza, a chocolate bar or a grid of squares and "
"asks which fraction was eaten, is left or is coloured, from halves to "
"twelfths and more than a whole."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.nacho.fastmath.metainfo.xml:41
msgid ""
"Fast Math remembers which arithmetic facts you answer wrong or slowly. "
"Practice rounds have no clock and ask those facts more often, and show the "
"right answer after a mistake. The progress view shows a grid of the facts of "
"each operation, coloured from strong to weak."
msgstr ""

